  "_note": "Combat backgrounds (PixelLab, Logan 2026-09-28). A fight uses its location's backgrounds for its tier (the strongest enemy: boss > elite > regular), picked per fight when there's more than one. `slots` are where enemies' feet stand for 1, 2 or 3 enemies, as [x, y] fractions of the image, measured on the art so every enemy stands on the floor. `floor` is the flat ground feet may stand on ({x: [from, to], y: [from, to]} as fractions of the image, `avoid`: [x0, y0, x1, y1] spots on it that aren't, like a hole); each fight stands every enemy near its slot's x, nudged a little sideways and anywhere in that y band, on the floor (Logan, 2026-10-16: a little different each fight). `zoom` enlarges the image from its bottom edge (1 = cover the screen) to lift a floor that starts too low for the enemy row. A fight with no background here keeps the plain field and the default enemy row. `weather` draws weather over the background (PlayField): \"rain\" falls and splashes, \"snow\" floats down and settles, \"dust\" blows in gusts and lifts off the ground, all on the ground from `ground` (the y fraction of the image where the ground starts) down.",
